azgor schrieb:
> 
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.
> 
> [1]: Since the ya have the unID'd appearance as "bamboo arrow",
> shouldn't their symbol be the brown, for the wood items, instead of the
> metally cyan? Yes, they should. --Chilliwack

"Bamboo arrow" i think means they have a bamboo shaft, instead of the
wood shaft of a regular arrow. On the other hand, i could hardly care
less which colour ya are displayed with.

> [2]: The effects of light sources (not just candles) should be
> cumulative. i.e. if you have three lit lamps, you should be able to see
> further than if you have fewer. --rogza

Oh, that'd be nice.

> [3]: When asked what kind of scroll one wants to write with a magic
> marker, if answered "Elbereth", the game should give you a ?oSM
> --HanClinto

I don't think so. 

> [4]: If you're in a pit, you should be able to dig into an adjacent
> (non-wall) square and create another pit,[...]

These are two pretty weird ideas. I like them, but i think they could
become messy to code. How do you differentiate between "connected"
pits and "isolated" adjacent pits, e.g. two pits created by detonating
land mines in adjacent squares?

> [6]: YAFM when entering a used armor store: "This shop reminds you of a
> locker room" --Botje

Only as an alternative "abandoned shop" message.

> [7]: some small penalty for cavemen breaking illiterate conduct or
> using certain 'complex' tools --teabing

No enforcing arbitrary pseudo-conducts, please!

> [8]: New conduct "never wore clothing" and subsets "never wore body
> armour" --Yui

Why o why do people keep suggesting the conductification of Stupid
Ascension Tricks?

> [9]: Throwing a cloak, towel, robe, or similar at an enemy
> (close-range) should have a chance of blinding it temporarily.

Heh. Nice.

> [10]: (a)pplying a stethoscope to a door should allow you to hear
> what's on the other side (such as shops or special rooms). --JoshJ

I don't think that'd add very much to the game. Feels rather adomish,
too.

> [12]: When a pit is generated, have it generate if it is poisoned or
> not, so the status does not change later. --Hours_

AFAIK spiked pits are always poisoned, it's just a matter of chance
whether a poke poisons you or not.

> [13]: Sinks in the same room as an altar should have a (tiny) chance of
> providing (un)holy water --Botje

The holy water basins in churches aren't _sinks_.

> [14]: There should always be a guaranteed random instrument available
> before arriving at the castle. --aristotle73

No. An instrument is not strictly required for entering the castle.

> [15]: Using a scroll of enchant weapon while wielding an iron chain
> should produce a chain whip.

A useful whip-type weapon (neither bull whip nor rubber hose do weapon
damage to thick-skinned monsters) would be an interesting addition,
but
i'm not sure of this suggestion - to get a chain, you pretty much need
an iron golem, and it might require some messy extra code: currently,
iron chains are non-weapon objects and are entirely unaffected by
enchant scrolls.

